comments.text:
Machines on Machines needs this for its Videos and Findings pages (MoM epic MOM-b08bdd, Phase B task MOM-d29573, AnthusAI/Machines-on-Machines board; filed 2026-11-08). Concrete shape that would let MoM delete its HTML regrouping (`_grouped_by_section` in web/hooks.py) and the `count="500"` source include it uses to find each section's best items (a cap: a section whose best Reference ranks below the 500th is not shown on the page):

`::include{kind="references" select="recent" bucket="week" medium="video" groups="section" per="7,6,6,3" [section="A|B|..."]}`
- one group per section that has at least one matching Reference, placed by the position of its best Reference in the include's order (the shared rolling-week order), no cap on how far down that best Reference is;
- `per` as in the listing include's groups: a list whose last value repeats;
- References with no section are never grouped; `section="A|B"` (see the new filters story) limits grouping to the sections the site has pages for;
- markup: `<section class="home-page-reference-group" data-section="<label>" data-index="<i>" data-total="<all matching References in that section>"><ul class="home-page-grid" data-card="tile">...</ul></section>`; `data-total` lets a site write "More <section> videos…" only when there are more;
- every placed Reference is claimed in the page ledger; not pageable (`paged` with `groups` is a build error).
Cross-reference: PPY-a9402d (section any-of, notSection, notMedium; paged lists).
